Z||000000||MR2KLR||10-28-2001||08:25 AM||||<BR>Anybody ever put a fuel cell up front inplace of the spare? What is the largest that will fit? What fuel pump did you use? any pics of it?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||10-28-2001||12:51 PM||||Why do you want to move the fuel tank?  It's already in the safest place it could be and it certainly helps out with the weight distribution.  If you only want to add a little bit of weight up front, try relocating your battery there.  Much safer.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||10-28-2001||01:21 PM||||He's probably like me; not too happy with the current range of the tiny gas tank  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I'll be moving an additional fuel cell up front eventually, with a small pump to decant fuel into the main tank upon request  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||MR2KLR||10-28-2001||01:39 PM||||<BR>  I thin a fuel sell will be safer than the stock tin tank. as of now the car I want has a 2.5L 4-cyl it has a bad fuel pump by the time i'm done with it the car will have either a LS1 or a 3rd gen RX7 turbo rotary engine. so I will started by building up the fuel system and then only  upgradeing the pump when I do get the new engine in. and by useing a fuel cell and braided steel lines that end of it will be legal in NHRA, IDRC, SCCA and just about any others you can think of while the stock setup will not.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||10-28-2001||01:53 PM||||For racing purposes the factory location is ideal!!<P>If the fuel tank in a stock fiero is ruptured chances are your dead anyway. Center mounted tank is ideal for steady state cornering. I have seen some guys pull the stock tank and have it retro fitted with newer fittings to meet fuel delivery purposes. I have never heard of SCCA requiring a different fuel tank in a Fiero. With an LS1 or turbo rotary engine in the car there are not many places you can race it really. Autocrossing in EM is one place , but the chassis of the Fiero will be easily outclassed no matter what engine you put in it, or what aftermarket parts you have under it.<P>If fuel delivery is your purpose , just swap in any number of other GM pumps that are designed to flow more than the stock Fiero pump.<P><BR>Just my .02 cents<P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, Big Bore TB, 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.<p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 10-28-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000005||maryjane||10-28-2001||01:53 PM||||Is it really that much trouble to stop for gas every couple hundred miles? Seems like a lot of trouble  & expense to add an extra fuel cell & pump. Of course, when ya get my age, nature calls about every couple hrs anyway on the open road, so I don't mind the stops. Probably has something to do with the gallons of coffee I drink while travelling. On the other hand, I watched the Red Green show where they wanted extra fuel capacity, so theyjust duct taped (the handy-man's friend) an old van to the roof of their car and ran a line from one tank to the other. "If ya can't be handsome to the ladies, at least be handy" is their motto. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 10-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||10-28-2001||01:54 PM||||For the ammount of trouble you are looking at.... Why don't you contact one of the companies that makes the cells about one that can fit in the OE location? A custom job may not be that much more expensive and you'll likely get a bigger cell in there.<P>At the same time you can change to an external fuel pump. That means no more tank dropping to service pumps.<P>Here's one maker. <A HREF="http://www.stable-energies.com/atl/atl.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.stable-energies.com/atl/atl.html</A> <P>you can also try searching for variations on this string (Minus quotes) "custom fuel cell bladder" in the various search engines.<P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-28-2001).]||||reg||1
