Z||000009||dennis_6||10-28-2001||07:55 PM||||I was also wondering about the external fuel pump.||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||10-28-2001||08:33 PM||||In the case of a fuel cell application, an external fuel pump simply goes into the fuel line heading to the engine. Electrically it simply splices to the existing harness. Just make sure the polarity is correct.<P>Exact type doesn't matter much. As long as you get on that can deliver the correct pressure, most of the pumps out there should flow enough volume for any street motor. (sans nitrous or turbo/super charge setups.) you can get various pumps, including the needed hardware, from nearly any speed shop, Summit, etc.<P>If you wanted an external pump with an OE tank... You'd need to yank the OE pump and figure out a new pickup screen but it's not rocket science. A number of old Ford, Chevy, etc pickup filters should be compatible. The one in my old Maverick just slid over a section of standard steel fuel line.||||reg||1
Z||000011||dennis_6||10-28-2001||08:50 PM||||Where can I find external fuel pumps that are in the fiero range 45-47 PSI and not the standard 7-15 PSI pumps?||||reg||5
